  "question": {
    "text": "Let $T_r$ be the rth term of an A.P. whose first term is a and common difference is $d$. If for some positive integers $m, n, m \\neq n, T_m=\\frac{1}{n}$ and $T_n=\\frac{1}{m}$, then $a-d$ equals",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5sDL8",
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "aLLid",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JmagO",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{mn}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aXcqX",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{m}+\\frac{1}{n}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\nT_m=\\frac{1}{n}=a+(m-1) d\n$$\nand $T_n=\\frac{1}{m}=a+(n-1) d$\nfrom (1) and (2) we get $a=\\frac{1}{m n}, \\quad d=\\frac{1}{m n}$ Hence $\\mathrm{a}-\\mathrm{d}=0$",
    "image": null
  },
